From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 04:09:13 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Log shader and pipeline compile times and pipeline waits

A frame hitch in a title can come from pipeline compiles, from the CPU
emulator translating code it has not run before, or from asset loads.
To tell them apart from a pulled log:

- the unix side logs, per call, the wall time and duration of every
  DXBC-to-AIR conversion (SM50Compile), MTLLibrary, MTLFunction and
  render or compute pipeline-state creation:
    [shader-time] HH:MM:SS.mmm <op> <ms> ms
- the d3d11 side logs each draw or dispatch that had to wait for its
  pipeline to finish compiling, and for how long, for graphics, compute,
  geometry-emulation and tessellation pipelines:
    [pso-wait] graphics|compute|geometry|tessellation <ms> ms
  A pipeline that is already compiled costs one atomic load, as before.

tools/perf.py reads both. The host app's release build logs neither:
[pso-wait] is at info level, below its DXMT_LOG_LEVEL=error, and
[shader-time], a bare stderr line, is skipped when MADEIRA_NO_DIAGNOSTICS is
set.

No unix call slot changes.

Class: diagnostics
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-09-25-hk-hitch-attribution.md
Offered-upstream: no
